---
kind: directory-reducer
args:
  brief: string
  context: ExperimentContext
  policy: ImprovementPolicy
returns: string
---
Plan one evidenced source change. context already contains the chosen parent's complete source, measured training evidence, exact opportunity classification and prior experiment outcomes. brief is a compact working card shown in your opening, containing source, measured costs and action patterns. Use it directly. Read context.history and context.lastExperiment together only when revising a rejected edit. Inspect an individual raw evidence or sourceFiles field only when the card is clipped or a specific uncertainty needs it; do not reprint the full context, discover known fields, or reread already observed data. Parent sampling and evidence collection have already been performed by exact code; do not reconstruct them or fetch the same data again.

Choose one coherent hypothesis predicting a measurable improvement toward policy.goal. Use actual modelTrace and serviceDeclarations. A fixture failure happened before the student ran; a timeout supplies an execution trace, not an observed wrong answer. Passing answers can still expose unnecessary model requests. The current .nl call is already a semantic computation: judge visible inputs here rather than creating another nl call for the same task, with code for exact aggregation and eval finish:true for atomic completion. A separate nl subcall is useful only for a real subproblem. Structural mode permits removing delegation, batching judgments and extracting exact helpers. Keep judgments semantic and use the actual service schema.

Use context.history and context.lastExperiment to revise a rejected approach. lastExperiment contains the actual edited source and its training trace, including failed actions; its validation fields are metrics, never answers. Diagnose why the edit failed rather than guessing from its headline score. Return the hypothesis as plain text; no tool or helper call is needed merely to return a semantic judgment. For cost or source-size objectives, an accepted improvement is a new starting point, not a reason to stop searching: pursue further evidenced simplification. If no further change is supported, return an empty string with return_result. Do not edit or execute target source, propose or evaluate candidates, or run experiments. The exact lifecycle executes your plan once; rejection is an outcome for the outer finite iteration.
